      "meta": {
        "description": "**Soria (Spain)** is an afforestation pilot site in Castile and León, covering approximately 42 ha across seven stands established between 1994 and 2020. The stands include holm oak, stone pine, Aleppo pine and Spanish juniper, planted on marginal limestone soils previously occupied by shrubland, grassland and low-productivity agricultural land. \n\nThe plots are managed and monitored by **CESEFOR**, a Spanish private non-profit foundation specialising in nature-based solutions for climate change mitigation and sustainable ecosystem management.",
        "attribution": {
          "text": "Data attribution not specified"
        },
        "categories": []
