      "meta": {
        "description": "**Vichada (Colombia)** is a large-scale reforestation and conservation pilot in the Orinoco River Basin, focused on above-ground biomass (AGB) estimation, ecosystem restoration and carbon sequestration. Approximately 35,000 ha of afforestation and conservation land provide reference areas, supported by around 1,000 monitoring plots and over 40,000 field measurement records. Tree species include Eucalyptus pellita, Pinus caribaea and Acacia mangium, established between 2007 and 2024. Field measurements of tree species, height, diameter at breast height (DBH) and measurement dates support the calibration and validation of Earth Observation (EO)-derived biomass products and long-term forest carbon monitoring.\n\n**Forliance** coordinates the pilot site and provides the relevant in-situ data. Forliance develops and manages nature-based climate projects, supporting companies in achieving their climate and environmental goals while contributing to the restoration and protection of forests and ecosystems.",
        "attribution": {
          "text": "Data attribution not specified"
        },
